<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">École William Ponty drama</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1937</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as a play</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Soundjata ou l'Epopée Mandingue (Djibril Tamsir Niane)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1960</span><span class="sg-chain-h">novelization of Djeli Mamoudou Kouyate's telling</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Sundiata: An Epic of Old Mali (G. D. Pickett)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1965</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Le Maître de la parole (Camara Laye)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1978</span><span class="sg-chain-h">novelization of Babou Condé's telling</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Soundjata, Le Lion (Issiaka Diakité-Kaba)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2010</span><span class="sg-chain-h">dramatized version, French and English</span></li></ul></section>
